<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Mideast live: Kuwait army says intercepting missile, drone attack from Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd9a656891ffddffcca319d2a3505c315b2287b99dfe345c4f6c6b98a929341b</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T03:08:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-mideast-live-kuwait-army-says-intercepting-missile-drone-attack-from-iran" /><summary type="html">Kuwait's army said Thursday it was intercepting a missile and drone attack from Iran, as Tehran targeted US allies in the Middle East. Iran has targeted US bases in Kuwait, Jordan, the United Arab Emirates, Bahrain and Iraq's autonomous Kurdistan region after extensive US bombardment on Tuesday of sites across the Islamic republic. Follow our liveblog for the latest developments.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran, US trade threats as Tehran blames Washington for wedding strike</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51d7762f0e540cff9af585f6e642490e497131c341ba7064d4c276a5d270fede</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T01:22:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-iran-us-trade-threats-wedding-strike" /><summary type="html">Iran and the United States traded threats on Wednesday after their heaviest military exchanges in weeks. Tehran accused Washington of striking a wedding party and called the attack a war crime. President Donald Trump threatened further US strikes, while Iran’s security chief warned Washington would face a “new strategy.”</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Minneapolis apartment shooting leaves three dead, multiple injured</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:004ee29f9acbb44a12260e8431a598e64c8034599eb13e49c3bcdaf456ccedc8</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T00:01:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260903-minneapolis-apartment-shooting" /><summary type="html">Two people were killed and a suspect died after a shooting at a downtown Minneapolis apartment building on Wednesday, police said. Three police officers were injured, including two who suffered gunshot wounds, and were in stable condition. One victim died at the scene and another at a hospital.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine warns Russian airspace ‘not safe’ in message to UN aviation watchdog</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:010d57b7f5f46e0cfb488d0ad151d675117924e63a563978e499eb14e9fa4595</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T22:46:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-un-civilian-flight-safety-russian-airspace-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Ukraine urged the UN aviation agency to call for a full ban on flights through Russian airspace, after President Volodymyr Zelensky warned it was becoming unsafe. Kyiv plans increased retaliation against intensified Russian strikes but would target only military facilities, Zelensky said, citing growing Ukrainian drone activity over Russia.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Palantir CEO Alex Karp says French restrictions on US software are ‘backfiring’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:31f733ffdc017a29dbf77ad969da79f41771f62f48a92ad9a11aa5bb0c387f2f</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T22:13:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20260902-palantir-france-digital-sovereignty" /><summary type="html">Palantir CEO Alex Karp said on Wednesday French restrictions limiting government use of US-made software were proving counterproductive. His comments followed France’s decision to replace Palantir with domestic provider ChapsVision at intelligence agency DGSI over data sovereignty concerns. Karp said Europe’s regulatory environment was hurting competitiveness.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>Venice Film Festival opens with George Clooney, Murdoch film and geopolitics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da84b34773c422ceb0f4dd2569d25444e52b174c177b461a85b59bbabdf13291</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T22:11:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/culture/20260902-venice-film-festival-clooney-murdoch-film-geopolitics" /><summary type="html">George Clooney used a Venice Film Festival appearance on Wednesday to weigh in on artificial intelligence, media ownership and US politics while receiving a lifetime achievement award. Clooney warned Hollywood must adapt to AI and criticised growing billionaire control of major media platforms.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Malta acquits tycoon Yorgen Fenech in investigative journalist murder case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b899a57a9b679814b15aceaac7766a17a6a4a6e16c4eaf69b0b3426a6e43e904</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T21:56:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-reporter-murder" /><summary type="html">A Maltese court on Wednesday acquitted tycoon Yorgen Fenech of orchestrating the 2017 car-bomb killing of investigative journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia, a verdict that drew condemnation from her family and press freedom advocates. Her family said the acquittal denied Caruana Galizia justice, while her son called it a “terrible decision.”</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Is Wintour still en vogue? Met navigates rough seas as Galliano retrospective sinks into 'Horizons'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91a8a356568fcb8f0fc66eda1a0367cd2a67b5fc96bc7336a405f52b125420be</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T21:39:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260902-is-wintour-still-en-vogue-the-met-navigates-rough-seas-as-galliano-s-horizons-sparks-controversy" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Dana Thomas, author of Gods and Kings: The Rise and Fall of Alexander McQueen and John Galliano, and the New York Times bestseller Deluxe: How Luxury Lost Its Luster. The fiery controversy over the Met's now-cancelled John Galliano retrospective challenges the timeless debate over whether art can be separated from the artist. Our guest argues that the key issue is institutional power. From her perspective, Galliano’s stature as an artist and fashion designer is never in dispute. All the while, his character has been once again very publicly called into question.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Outrage as Maltese tycoon acquitted of reporter Daphne Caruana Galizia's murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d4563e3d63cbe2e2203bf4b1b4392a8969fb11248fee7b4fdc3c8b7feed96361</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T21:20:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-of-reporter-daphne-caruana-galizia-s-murder" /><summary type="html">A Maltese court on Wednesday acquitted tycoon Yorgen Fenech of orchestrating the car-bomb killing of investigative reporter Daphne Caruana Galizia, sparking outrage from her family and media freedom advocates. The wealthy businessman had stood accused of masterminding the 2017 assassination of 53-year-old Caruana Galizia, which sparked unprecedented protests and brought down a government. MaltaToday Executive Editor Kurt Sansone speaks with FRANCE 24.</summary></entry><entry><title>US-Iran war: Old videos falsely claim to show new attacks on American bases</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c0afac6229ea85dabf46c395c0b75825f53180f64e5af117a2e0f56772fc779b</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T20:57:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-iran-war-old-videos-falsely-claim-to-show-new-attacks-on-american-bases-1" /><summary type="html">As US-Iran hostilities flare up and strikes has resumed, so has a wave of misinformation online. Old and unrelated videos are flooding social media, falsely presented as footage of new attacks. As tensions escalate, lips filmed in Dubai, Russia and the US have been misrepresented as Iranian strikes on US bases in the Gulf. Another 68-year-old video of a US nuclear test has been falsely claimed to show Iran detonating mines in the Strait of Hormuz. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>US oversees signing of ‘billions’ in deals between Venezuela and Chevron, ENI, GE</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f6731abd5960ec0dba8109b4b5ec617faf0f0d540443d89692a2673d0b41851</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T20:54:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260902-us-oversees-signing-of-billions-in-deals-between-venezuela-and-chevron-eni-ge" /><summary type="html">US oil giant Chevron, Italy's ENI and GE Vernova signed deals worth "tens of billions of dollars" with Venezuela, US Energy Secretary Chris Wright said Wednesday during a trip to Caracas where he and Interim President Delcy Rodriguez finalised the agreements.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Kenyan editor found safe after abduction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:512b907cfdab37bbc93706f8dab064306828b5c4281d7b139729e3c7c4d7f43e</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T20:15:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenyan-editor-found-safe-after-abduction" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, rights groups in Kenya call for an investigation after a top journalist is abducted overnight  by heavily armed men. Also, trials for three potential vaccines against the Bunjeebuyyoo strain of Ebola are due to start over the next couple of months. And Senegalese consumers who are frustrated by the rising cost of living have launched a new campaign.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Chevron, Eni commit to expand oil projects in Venezuela under US eye</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46bb66d6451b989744d9b9f773b31e970b0fa93403a4f796b696ddc6b628f6dc</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T20:00:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/chevron-eni-commit-to-expand-oil-projects-in-venezuela-under-us-eye" /><summary type="html">U.S.' Chevron, Italy's Eni and other foreign energy producers committed on Wednesday to major project expansions to boost oil output in Venezuela, in a signing ceremony in Caracas overseen by interim President ​Delcy Rodriguez and ‌U.S. Energy Secretary Chris Wright. FRANCE 24's Maya Yataghene reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zelensky warns airlines Russian skies not safe due to Ukraine drones</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94ebd220c6f8111388d0224ab377d3dc855d7e345f4295ccf15caa952ffac46a</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T19:32:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/zelensky-warns-airlines-russian-skies-not-safe-due-to-ukraine-drones" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky warned Tuesday that his country's drones would make Russia's airspace "completely unsafe" for the duration of the war, drawing accusations of "state terrorism" from Russian leader Vladimir Putin. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Former British Military Intelligence Officer Philip Ingram explains that Zelensky's warning is addressed to "those international airlines from the Middle East, from South East Asia, China included that are still operating into Moscow" adding that "it's all part of the information war and bringing the overall conflict to the Russian people".</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Spanish report flags Moroccan police's 'total permissiveness' in Ceuta migrant rush</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abbf610219ec52d2f49944ff2ede9819a442a1f990ebccc9b811ea7d70e3939e</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T19:23:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260902-spanish-report-flags-moroccan-police-s-total-permissiveness-in-ceuta-migrant-rush--02ef226c47f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260902-spanish-report-flags-moroccan-police-s-total-permissiveness-in-ceuta-migrant-rush" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish report flags Moroccan police's 'total permissiveness' in Ceuta migrant rush</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:372491ee533db8e196c2321fc0a51b2cc8605965b2079dfccc5b5f97dd4b55b7</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T19:20:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260902-spanish-report-flags-moroccan-police-s-total-permissiveness-in-ceuta-migrant-rush--02ef226c47f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260902-spanish-report-flags-moroccan-police-s-total-permissiveness-in-ceuta-migrant-rush" /><summary type="html">Moroccan security forces displayed "total permissiveness" during last month's massive wave of migrants who crossed into the Spanish North African territory of Ceuta, according to a Spanish police report seen by a French news agency on Wednesday.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Macron and Charles III visit historic Bayeux tapestry exhibition together</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b5f01754d8c5ca99da6533669bb74087e7a3b95ed257ecdd9a70085c6eaf14a</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T18:09:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-france-s-macron-in-britain-to-help-unveil-bayeux-tapestry--e5685b353904.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-france-s-macron-in-britain-to-help-unveil-bayeux-tapestry" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli FM Gideon Sa'ar: 'I hope Iran will not make the mistake of attacking us'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f5a8e8cbd1befdf81310a60b49f42ebdc5856c2193b58916a96b2eda1928765</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T17:49:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20260902-israeli-fm-gideon-sa-ar-i-hope-iran-will-not-make-the-mistake-of-attacking-us--4ec8673d7440.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260902-israeli-fm-gideon-sa-ar-i-hope-iran-will-not-make-the-mistake-of-attacking-us" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Israel's Minister of Foreign Affairs Gideon Sa’ar addressed the resumption in fighting between the US and Iran, and warned that any Iranian attack on Israel would trigger a "severe" response. He also accused Tehran of continuing to pursue "nuclear weapons aspirations", claiming that Israel "will not allow" Iran to achieve them.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Videos and debris raise questions over alleged US strike on Iranian wedding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9142de844bbbb35cdc5795f9d9bb521575bc123cd724c9ef49e03b273dad77ae</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T17:31:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-videos-and-debris-raise-questions-over-alleged-us-strike-on-iranian-wedding--89b2ba4b7915.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-videos-and-debris-raise-questions-over-alleged-us-strike-on-iranian-wedding" /><summary type="html">On the evening of September 1, a barrage of US missile and drone attacks on a town in southern Iran allegedly struck a wedding ceremony, killing at least five people, including a four-year-old boy. FRANCE 24 geolocated a direct hit to the civilian building where local residents say the wedding was being held. The building was more than 135 meters from the apparent target, a communications tower.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Russia blamed for explosive-laden drone found at German airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c96e6c2bb6157bf6ac24be33aa4550121369ba7835401f8edce6b886c043be1</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T16:11:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-russia-blamed-for-explosive-laden-drone-found-at-german-airport--a786ed42be94.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-russia-blamed-for-explosive-laden-drone-found-at-german-airport" /><summary type="html">After #Germany blamed #Russia for the explosive-laden #drone found at #Leipzig airport on August 4, #Berlin has introduced new sanctions against #Moscow. Namely, its consulate in #Bonn and the Russian House - a cultural centre thought to be a Russian #spy hub - in #Berlin.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Trump suggests renaming Hormuz 'Trump Strait'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64bccab016bd8491a1f37d3f69e5c066606d1b0e7962e8583dbe5fb8da796b9d</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T15:37:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-us-military-striking-targets-in-iran-after-attempted-attacks-on-shipping--2a2323f6d3bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-us-military-striking-targets-in-iran-after-attempted-attacks-on-shipping" /></entry><entry><title>Egypt welcomes Xi as Beijing expands influence in region</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00c4df03fbf2681513ddfbc156034dac1ecf37569059be5d906daf18e8ca9a35</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T15:33:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-egypt-welcomes-xi-as-beijing-expands-influence-in-region--d47229693cee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-egypt-welcomes-xi-as-beijing-expands-influence-in-region" /><summary type="html">Egyptian ​President Abdel Fattah al-Sisi welcomed China's Xi Jinping to Cairo on Wednesday, opening a visit that highlights Cairo's deepening ties with Beijing as regional turmoil prompts U.S. allies to reassess longstanding security relationships.</summary></entry><entry><title>Philippine couple married in hip-deep floodwaters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2bb7dce73a061df5c7cb29285547b821198b29098e94ecc5c38644442b76a36b</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T15:21:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-philippine-couple-married-in-hip-deep-floodwaters--6777e4d8da7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-philippine-couple-married-in-hip-deep-floodwaters" /><summary type="html">A Philippine couple tied the knot on Tuesday at a Catholic church swamped in hip-deep waters, as heavy rains had pummelled large parts of the country for a month.</summary></entry><entry><title>US postal whistleblower warns thousands of midterm ballots could be lost</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ded47238951cb6ab1be1110c5046281086490de850b35688757a37d87813f60</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T15:17:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-us-postal-whistleblower-warns-thousands-of-midterm-ballots-could-be-lost--ca7fa2750ae5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-us-postal-whistleblower-warns-thousands-of-midterm-ballots-could-be-lost" /><summary type="html">A US Postal Service whistleblower has warned that millions of Americans could be prevented from receiving mail ballots ahead of November's midterm elections because of a rushed, new system ordered by President Donald Trump and due for launch Tuesday. Trump signed an executive order in March seeking tighter controls on mail voting, which he has repeatedly claimed is vulnerable to widespread fraud despite offering no evidence of misconduct on such a scale. France 24’s Kethevane Gorjestani takes a closer look.</summary></entry></feed>
